# Caddy in front of the fork API: HTTPS on 443 straight to 127.0.0.1:18901, replacing Tailscale
# Funnel for it (in the load test Funnel failed 19% of requests at 200 visitors; the VM itself
# failed none). Installed by infra/executor/caddy/setup.sh. The host name is FORK_API_HOST from
# /etc/thesis/caddy.env; Caddy gets and renews its certificate by itself (TLS-ALPN on 443).
# It listens on FORK_API_BIND, the VM's own address (setup.sh finds it), not on every address:
# Tailscale holds 443 on its own interface while Funnel is on.
#
# The fork API counts each visitor by the last X-Forwarded-For entry when the request comes from
# loopback (scripts/fork/api/guard.ts). Caddy ignores what a client sends in that header and sets
# it to the address it saw, so the per-IP limits can't be spoofed.
{
	servers {
		timeouts {
			read_header 10s
			idle 2m
		}
	}
}

{$FORK_API_HOST} {
	bind {$FORK_API_BIND}
	encode zstd gzip
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:18901
}
